{title: Auld Lang Syne}
{artist: Robert Burns}
{key: G}
{rhythm: Ballad}
{license: public_domain}
{rights_holder: Public Domain}
{source: Scots Musical Museum, 1796 (Traditional Scottish air)}

Should [G]auld acquaintance [D]be forgot,
And [G]never brought to [C]mind?
Should [G]auld acquaintance [D]be forgot,
And [C]days of [D]auld lang [G]syne?

For auld lang [D]syne, my dear,
For [G]auld lang [C]syne,
We'll [G]tak a cup o' [D]kindness yet,
For [C]auld [D]lang [G]syne.

And [G]surely ye'll be [D]your pint-stowp!
And [G]surely I'll be [C]mine!
And [G]we'll tak a cup o' [D]kindness yet,
For [C]auld [D]lang [G]syne.

